cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "echo-lineage: verification, signed decisions, and bounded local handoff"
message: "Cite Robert Jordan as the project pseudonym, together with the repository and exact commit used; this is not attribution to a separate person."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Robert Jordan (project pseudonym)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/robertjordan1990/echo-lineage"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - agent provenance
  - lineage verification
  - handoff evidence
  - explicit acceptance
  - local context consumption
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A transport-neutral protocol with a read-only verifier that separates
  consistency checks for lineage and handoff evidence from acceptance, import,
  and activation. Stage 2B records scoped local operator decisions using pinned
  Ed25519 keys and never activates a runtime. The separate Stage 2C profile
  implements one bound source-to-recipient handoff, return receipts, selected
  verified-byte import, and separately authorized use by a fixed local UTF-8
  consumer. It does not integrate with or authenticate a cloud model. The
  Stage 2C RC1 research prerelease has completed technical review; human review
  of key and privilege semantics remains pending and does not require real
  keys. Actual key provisioning is a separate decision.
  Maintained under the project pseudonym Robert Jordan and developed through
  documented human–AI collaboration within fAIR DecentrAIzation. The pseudonym
  does not identify a separate person or assign copyright ownership. This
  publication snapshot makes no priority claim and does not establish a date
  of first invention. Stage 2A does not authenticate actors or import state.
